{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he took a burnt-offering and sacrifices.</b> These are the shelamim." "And the sense of \"to Elohim\" is that now he began to have the honored name as Elohim." "<b>And Aaron came, and all the elders of Israel.</b> And there is no need to mention Moses, for they were in his tent." "<b>To eat bread.</b> Shelamim." "<b>And the sense of \"before the Elohim.\"</b> For the tent of Moses was on the east side of the tent of meeting."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:32.300693602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}